; The first rule that matches. First how many rules each letter has a verdict for; then for each letter, left's and
; right's verdicts on each rule side by side (1 a context matches, 0 not) in; out the number of the first rule whose
; contexts both match (the first rule that matches wins), -1 if none does.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03                    INP   rules    03-03: the verdicts a letter
  04            let     CLA   m1       04-24: a letter's verdicts
  05                    STO   ch
  06                    CLA   z
  07                    STO   r
  08            each    INP   a
  09                    INP   b
  10                    CLA   ch
  11                    TAC   chk
  12                    JMP   nx
  13            chk     CLA   a
  14                    ADD   b
  15                    SUB   n2
  16                    TAC   nx
  17                    CLA   r
  18                    STO   ch
  19            nx      CLA   r
  20                    ADD   00
  21                    STO   r
  22                    SUB   rules
  23                    TAC   each
  24                    OUT   ch
  25                    JMP   let
  30            rules   DATA  0
  31            ch      DATA  0
  32            r       DATA  0
  33            a       DATA  0
  34            b       DATA  0
  35            z       DATA  0
  36            m1      DATA  -1
  37            n2      DATA  2
